<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="If you can't make a shift">
        <ol>
            <li>On <strong>Upcoming shifts</strong>, find the shift and select <strong>Can't make it</strong>.</li>
            <li>Say why, then select <strong>Tell my manager</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Your manager decides. Until they do, you're still on the shift, so if it's urgent, call them as
            well. If they let you off, the shift becomes an open shift and everyone who could work it is told.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Swapping a shift">
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Ask to swap</strong> on the shift, add a note for colleagues if you like, and select
                <strong>Ask for swaps</strong>.</li>
            <li>Colleagues who could work it are told. They can offer one of their own shifts in return.</li>
            <li>Offers appear under <strong>Your requests</strong> on the <strong>Up for grabs</strong> tab. Select
                <strong>Swap</strong> on the one you want.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Depending on how your venue is set up, the swap happens straight away or a manager approves it
            first. To help someone else, look under <strong>Swaps you could help with</strong>, pick
            <strong>Your shift to give in return</strong> and select <strong>Offer this swap</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Picking up open shifts">
        <FluentText>
            Shifts nobody is on yet are listed under <strong>Open shifts</strong> on the Up for grabs tab, and you
            get a notification when a new one comes up.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Pick up this shift</strong>: the first person to pick it up gets it.</li>
            <li><strong>Ask for this shift</strong>: a manager chooses who gets it. Your request shows as
                <strong>Asked for</strong> until then.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            Some positions need training before you can work them. If you're missing a course, the shift
            says which one, with a button to go to it. If the course hasn't been assigned to you, ask your
            manager.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <FluentText>
        Changes can only be asked for on published shifts that haven't started. You can withdraw a
        request from the Up for grabs tab while it's still waiting.
    </FluentText>
</HelpTab>
